It uses:

- Readium's Go toolkit (https://github.com/readium/go-toolkit), BSD 3-Clause, for EPUB: v0.16.1 with its remote
  archives, fetchers and assets (S3, Google Cloud Storage, HTTP) left out, files removed and none changed
  (experiments/02-crengine-go/trim-gotoolkit.sh).
- Blitz (https://github.com/DioxusLabs/blitz), under the MIT License, with Parley, HarfRust and ICU4X (MIT, Apache
  License 2.0 or the Unicode License), for laying out and drawing pages. Blitz is built with three changes of ours, in
  engine/patches/: lines outside the page skipped when painting (blitz-cull-lines.patch), pictures decoded when
  drawn, at the size drawn (blitz-lazy-images.patch), and a right-to-left list's bullets on its right
  (blitz-rtl-markers.patch). Parley 0.12.0 is built with one change, in engine/patches/: a
  line's trailing space moved to the line's end, Unicode's bidi rule L1 (parley-trailing-whitespace.patch, taken from
  https://github.com/linebender/parley/pull/907, not yet merged there).
- Stylo, Firefox's CSS engine, inside Blitz, and Symphonia, for decoding narration's audio, under the Mozilla Public
  License 2.0, unchanged: their source is on crates.io and at https://github.com/servo/stylo and
  https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia.
- Every library built into the reader, with its licence and copyright notices: licenses/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md in
  each package, made by reader/scripts/licenses.sh.
- The fonts, unchanged: Parastoo (copyright 2015 Saber Rastikerdar), Vazirmatn (copyright 2015 The Vazirmatn Project Authors),
  Frank Ruhl Libre (copyright 2015 The Frank Ruhl Libre Project Authors) and Noto Naskh Arabic (copyright 2022 The
  Noto Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1, and DejaVu (copyright 2003 Bitstream, Inc., and the DejaVu changes in the public domain),
  the Bitstream Vera licence: in reader/fonts, each with its licence.

On a Kobo it is started from a row in Kobo's More tab, a launcher of ours inside Kobo's interface whose way in and
row painting are adapted from NickelModManager (https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/NickelModManager, copyright 2026 Nico
Verbruggen, MIT License: its licence is in licenses/LICENSE-NickelModManager.md in the Kobo package, and in
reader/kobo/launcher/LICENSE-NickelModManager.txt).

On a Kindle it is started by a launcher of ours from the Kindle's own library.
